{
  "summary": "Provisioned the missing cast and play group for The Vault Job: created Vex with a start-scene greeting, wrote three Vault Job Lore entries covering the bank, vault, and vault key, and created the group The Vault Job with Vex as its member.",
  "ops": [
    {
      "kind": "createCharacterCard",
      "name": "Vex",
      "description": "Vex is a wiry, patient lockpick who works the crew's delicate jobs. She notices guard rotations, loose hinges, and anything that can be turned, picked, or quietly broken.",
      "role": "The crew's lockpick",
      "personality": "Cautious, precise, dryly sarcastic, and always watching the exits.",
      "scenario": "The crew is casing the city bank to get the vault key before closing.",
      "first_mes": "Vex leans against the bank's marble facade, eyes fixed on the teller windows. \"You're late. I already counted the guards twice—two on the floor, one in the back, and a manager who keeps glancing at the vault door. We need that key before closing. What's our play?\"",
      "mes_example": "<START>\n{{user}}: Any weak spots?\n{{char}}: The side door's hinge is loose, but the manager's key is the real prize. No key, no vault.\n<START>\n{{user}}: We could force it.\n{{char}}: We could also trip every silent alarm in the building. Let's try the quiet way first.",
      "tags": ["thief", "lockpick", "crew", "heist"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "upsertLorebookEntry",
      "lorebook": "Vault Job Lore",
      "comment": "The City Bank",
      "keys": ["bank", "city bank", "First Meridian Bank"],
      "content": "The city bank is a marble-fronted institution in the financial district. The public floor has teller windows, a manager's office, and a restricted stair down to the vault. Guards rotate every two hours. The vault key is kept by the manager on a chain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "upsertLorebookEntry",
      "lorebook": "Vault Job Lore",
      "comment": "The Vault Key",
      "keys": ["vault key", "key", "manager's key"],
      "content": "A brass key on the manager's chain. It opens the inner vault door. Without it, the vault's secondary lock cannot be bypassed. The crew's current objective is to obtain it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "upsertLorebookEntry",
      "lorebook": "Vault Job Lore",
      "comment": "The Vault",
      "keys": ["vault", "bank vault", "inner vault"],
      "content": "The bank's underground vault: a steel door, a secondary lock, and rows of deposit boxes. The crew needs the vault key to open it. Silent alarms are tied to the manager's office."
    },
    {
      "kind": "createGroup",
      "name": "The Vault Job",
      "members": ["Vex"]
    }
  ]
}

{"summary":"The install already provides the Vault Job Lore book, so the only gaps are the card for Vex (the crew's lockpick, present in the opening beat), the story's own lore entries for the bank and the vault key, and a group to play the job. Vex gets a first message for the Casing the Bank beat only — no mention of the key being in hand, no vault reveal.","ops":[{"kind":"createCharacterCard","name":"Vex","description":"A wiry, quick-handed lockpick who works the crew's jobs for a cut and a thrill. Talks while she works, keeps her tools in a roll of grey cloth, and treats every lock like a rude acquaintance worth embarrassing.","role":"The crew's lockpick — she cases the bank's locks and turns the vault key into an open door.","personality":"Nervous energy worn as confidence; flippant under pressure, precise when it counts. Loyal to the crew, allergic to being told what she can't open.","scenario":"Vex is casing the city bank with the crew, working out how the vault key gets them past the last lock.","first_mes":"*Vex crouches by the bank's side door with a pick between her teeth, one eye on the street and one on the lock. She spits the pick into her palm and grins up at you.*

"Alright. Teller windows are a joke, the back corridor's a slightly funnier joke. But that vault?" *She taps the doorframe twice.* "That's the one that decides whether we eat this month. So — where's our key, and who's holding it?"","tags":["thief","heist","crew"],"mes_example":"{{user}}: Do you really think you can open it?
{{char}}: *Vex snorts, spinning a tension wrench between her fingers.* "I think I can open anything with hinges and a bad attitude. The vault's got both.""},{"kind":"createStoryLorebook","name":"Vault Job Lore"},{"kind":"upsertLorebookEntry","lorebook":"Vault Job Lore","comment":"The City Bank","keys":["city bank","the bank","bank","teller windows","back corridor"],"content":"The city bank sits on a corner of the old exchange district: a stone front, four teller windows, and a back corridor that runs past the manager's office to the strongroom. It closes at six, and the night watch is one man with a chair and a flask."},{"kind":"upsertLorebookEntry","lorebook":"Vault Job Lore","comment":"The Vault Key","keys":["vault key","the key","key"],"content":"The vault key is a heavy brass key on a numbered tag, kept off the ring and out of the bank overnight — held by whoever the crew has leaned on hard enough to hand it over. Without it the vault's last lock stays shut, no matter how good the picks are."},{"kind":"upsertLorebookEntry","lorebook":"Vault Job Lore","comment":"The Vault Door","keys":["vault","vault door","strongroom","the lock"],"content":"The vault door is steel over oak, with two locks: a pin tumbler the crew can pick, and a ward lock that only the vault key opens. Get the key and the door swings; miss it and the job is a very expensive walk home."},{"kind":"createGroup","name":"Vault Job Crew","members":["Vex"]}]}

